{"id": "EUVD-2026-32447", "enisaUuid": "a37ce47f-b8fe-3a36-a324-88add8ccd063", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: defio: Disconnect deferred I/O from the lifetime of struct fb_info\n\nHold state of deferred I/O in struct fb_deferred_io_state. Allocate an\ninstance as part of initializing deferred I/O and remove it only after\nthe final mapping has been closed. If the fb_info and the contained\ndeferred I/O meanwhile goes away, clear struct fb_deferred_io_state.info\nto invalidate the mapping. Any access will then result in a SIGBUS\nsignal.\n\nFixes a long-standing problem, where a device hot-unplug happens while\nuser space still has an active mapping of the graphics memory. The hot-\nunplug frees the instance of struct fb_info. Accessing the memory will\noperate on undefined state.", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:57:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:26:42", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4aab89603b637a2e441b38808c4f6fe7d1184df6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fda0d6b45faad44926dd3e4f55f118d899b2e27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a40f8bc9bb713329f1c35ffc199ee961a7135b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b53d3a52e8e5403a4f4fb57ac6cad3fd2cb1066", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25c2b77bc463f29ee71a54b883548baf9386a0db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0aafb421dd15e935d81543152617f2742cefa70", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ded47ad003f09a94b6a710b5c47f4aa5ceb7429"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w279-mj9j-w893", "CVE-2026-46065"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0047abff-a46c-3240-a060-618ec5caabbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.22"}, {"id": "0db46d4b-c1e6-37cd-ab9f-3ad245cd5128", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "20213f32-9b37-32